#TITLE LNTYPE 2 Continuous Long Note
#SUBTITLE MGQ-style long notes spelled as a run of repeated tokens
#ARTIST be-music
#GENRE TEST
#BPM 120
#PLAYLEVEL 2
#TOTAL 250
#DIFFICULTY 2

*---------------------- EXTENDED HEADER FIELD
* `#LNTYPE 1` pairs a head and a tail object; `#LNTYPE 2` instead spells a long
* note as an unbroken RUN of the same object ID across consecutive slots, and the
* long note lasts from the first token of the run to the end of the last one.
* Every token after the first is a continuation and must not trigger a keysound.
*
* The three cases below are the ones that separate a correct type-2 expander
* from a naive one:
*
*   measure 1 - a single run inside one measure
*   measure 2 - two runs in the same measure separated by an empty slot, which
*               must stay two long notes rather than one
*   measures 3-4 - a run that continues across the measure boundary
*
* `ln-mode-1-long-note.bms` covers the same lanes with `#LNTYPE 1` / `#LNOBJ`,
* so the two files together cover both spellings of a long note.

#PLAYER 1
#LNTYPE 2
#LNMODE 1

*---------------------- RESOURCES FIELD

#WAV01 sample.wav
#WAV02 branch.wav
#WAV03 right.wav

